{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/74513-really-stupidly-obvious-question-re-making-monsters","id":74513,"title":"Really stupidly obvious question re: Making Monsters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-18T13:28:50-08:00","id":74513,"title":"Really stupidly obvious question re: Making Monsters","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> I'm about to kick off my Hunter game (it's a larp but don't hold that against me...) and I'm wondering what is the best resource/book/site/blog/parchment/rock slab to show me how to create Monsters? Something like the Zombie creation rules in Antagonists but less specific. Is it just as simple as going through the God Machine, pulling numbers out of my nether regions, and adding some Dread Powers out of H:tV? 'Cause that sounds a little (actually, a lot) arbitrary, and I'm not sure I know the system inside-out enough to create interesting, challenging, but not overwhelming monsters, especially in regards to things like Defence, Wound Levels, attack pools and damage modifiers.<br /> <br /> For some examples of the types of things I'm looking to create: (Oh by the way: If you're playing in the Dunedin's Vigil larp, look no further!!! Here There Be DAGRONS)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">- An animated tree that shoots flower &quot;bullets&quot;<br /> - A dragon (yep, I was serious about the warning <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), newly hatched from a stone egg<br /> - A psychically-endowed human with a penchant for Domination<br /> - A cult who are trying to summon and bind something to give them power (for this one I'm probably going to use normal humans for the cultists, and a Demon from H:tV as the summoned thing</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And many, many, <b>many</b> more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks folks,<br /> Viperion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T17:11:10-08:00","id":75328,"title":"","content":"Wow have I really stumped everyone?<br /> <br /> How do you guys stat out your monsters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T20:28:08-08:00","id":75414,"title":"","content":"It may seem arbitrary but I use Dread Powers.<br /> It depends on the creature they're facing, but if you fully stat out everything players might come across, you're going to burn yourself out or, at least, do a lot of work for nothing.<br /> Are the players going to try talking to the bullet-shooting tree? Would it understand? Does it have thought processes beyond 'something is near, shoot?' Maybe, but it's reasonable to think that it wouldn't. So you don't need mental or social stats, or skills, and you don't need to dole out merits.<br /> Generally if something is definitely going to see combat, you figure out some appropriate stats (you'll need the character sheets, so you can see what you're dealing with and you don't create a monster you want to be scary but can't hurt them because they're all wearing kevlar all the time). Then you add some dread powers or equivalent things. Your bullet tree wouldn't necessarily be dealing with dexterity+firearms. So you give it a base dicepool for shooting (shoot+blastdreadpower, or something), or you can give it a dicepool for shooting but use the stats for a particular gun that it shoots like, so you add the damage and piercing or range of that gun onto the dicepool.<br /> You can see stuff like that in the first rulebooks, where an example NPC just has a dicepool for something like, 'dirty fighting' or 'finding information.'<br /> That's good for other things, too, like your dragon probably can't do much except try and scare things and breathe fire, so you give it dicepools for those two things, and when you require a defense (if the players try animal ken'ing it or dominating it) you pick something appropriate. The dicepools don't have to be combat-related.<br /> <br /> Then lets say your dominator character, he's canny and vindictive, with an instinct for survival. So you might want to stat him out more, if he's going to be a reoccurring thorn in the sides of the players, and you can either give him a full sheet of character abilities, you can use powers from other books, or dread powers, they're pretty much the same thing.<br /> <br /> Here's a link to some information I've used, but only a couple times as I only found it recently:<br /> <a href=\"http://worldofdarkness.wikia.com/wiki/Quick_NPCs_(nWoD\" target=\"_blank\">http://worldofdarkness.wikia.com/wiki/Quick_NPCs_(nWoD</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T00:49:50-08:00","id":75472,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Dread Powers are pretty solid, and great for making all sorts of customized weird things. The way DP's are written is usually broad/vague enough that you can apply a hundred different spooky flavorings to any one power.<br /> <br /> I even use it to make pretty much any monster type that isn't a part of the game I'm playing even outside of Hunter, like say if I want werewolves in a Vampire:the Requiem game, but I don't want all the baggage of Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T15:44:02-08:00","id":75924,"title":"","content":"Hunter the Vigil style dread powers for enemies in the flesh. For spirits I use the Book of Spirits simply because it is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T15:32:22-08:00","id":77850,"title":"","content":"OK so I had a go at statting up one of these things. Let me know what you think of it - the idea is the first fight against it will be a bit of a surprise, and then if/when they fight it again, they'll be able to overcome it. This is for starting level, Tier 1 hunter cells. Again, if you're playing in Dunedin's Vigil, please don't read this!!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Int 2, Wits 1, Res 4 </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Str 6, Dex 3, Sta 5 , </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Pre 2, Man 1, Cmp 4 </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Skills: Brawl 3, Firearms 3<br /> Merits: Demolisher 1, Hardy 3, Iron Will, Iron Skin 4<br /> Dread Powers: Crushing Blow, Dread Attack 2 (Bullets)</span></span><br /> <br /> Willpower: 8<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Defence: 4 (In this game I'm using Brawl or Weaponry to determine defence, not Athletics)<br /> Size: 8 Health: 13</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Amour: 3/1, but see also Iron Skin Merit</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Attack pools: Flower Bullets: 6, +2L damage. Branch swing 9, Lethal damage (after spending WP for CBlow)</span></span></span> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Thoughts?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":568,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","user":"Viperion","date":".  Added Willpower, Defence and corrected Armor 02-23-2014, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:31:13-08:00","id":80465,"title":"","content":"Must be really bad <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's OK guys, I can take it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:17:43-08:00","id":80743,"title":"","content":"It's fine, though obviously how well it'll perform will depend on the player characters. The branch swing could theoretically kill a player in one shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 